{
  "category": "Whiskers Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "WHISCASH is extremely territorial. Just one of these POKéMON will claim a large pond as its exclusive territory. If a foe approaches it, it thrashes about and triggers a massive earthquake.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "If WHISCASH goes on a wild rampage, it sets off a quake-like tremor with a radius of over three miles. This POKéMON has the ability to predict real earthquakes.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mysteriously, it can foretell earthquakes. In the daytime, it sleeps in mud at the bottom of a pond. When it awakens, it continually feeds throughout the night.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "It makes its nest at the bottom of swamps. It will eat anything - if it is alive, WHISCASH will eat it.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "It makes its nest at the bottom of swamps. It will eat anything - if it is alive, WHISCASH will eat it.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is very territorial. It repels foes by setting off tremors that extend over a three-mile radius.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "As a result of causing tremors by thrashing about, it developed the ability to foretell real quakes.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is extremely protective of its territory. If any foe approaches, it attacks using vicious tremors.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "It claims a large swamp to itself. If a foe comes near it, it sets off tremors by thrashing around.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "It claims a large swamp to itself. If a foe comes near it, it sets off tremors by thrashing around.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is extremely protective of its territory. If any foe approaches, it attacks using vicious tremors.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is extremely protective of its territory. If any foe approaches, it attacks using vicious tremors.",
      "version": "white"
